-5679-9557-81416d5dd1c3" :question/math-academy-id "q-135397" :question/problem "Find the inverse of the following matrix:\n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ \\sqrt{2} & 1 & 0 \\\\ -2 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Notice that we're given a Frobenius matrix:\n\n- all entries on the main diagonal are ones\n\n- the matrix has only one column (the $1$st column) where some entries below the main diagonal are not zeros\n\n- all the other entries outside the main diagonal are zeros\n\nTo find the inverse of a Frobenius matrix, we simply take the non-zero entries outside the main diagonal with opposite signs. \n\nIn our case, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}^{-1}={[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ \\sqrt{2} & 1 & 0 \\\\ -2 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]}^{-1}=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ -\\sqrt{2} & 1 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-135397/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "77673d0c-9f03-5915-b2ab-4a5d6cb2d94d"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-135397"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]}]
